{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-pachner-pentagon-borromean","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Conjecture","doco:Section"],"label":"conj:pachner-pentagon-borromean","kind":"conjecture","title":"Pachner $2$–$3$ move = Pentagon identity at Borromean ideal-tetrahedron decomposition","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-pentagon-uv-commutation","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-q-rogers-pentagon-archimedean","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/conj-quantum-dilogarithm-stratified","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-dilogarithm-disambiguation","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-borromean-baryon","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-atom-knot-exists","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-reeb-bundle-complement-equals-volume"],"cites":["references/pachner1991","references/adams1985hyperbolic","references/faddeev_kashaev1994","references/kashaev1997","references/turaev-viro1992","references/neumann-zagier1985"],"tags":["tier:S","pachner","pentagon","duality-d15","borromean","ideal-tetrahedron","tv-rt-state-sum","h4-closure-route","axiom-class","open-problem","conditional-on-class","quantum-dilogarithm"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean","text":"pachner-pentagon-borromean.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"conj:pachner-pentagon-borromean\"></a><p><em>The Pachner <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>–<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code> move on the ideal-tetrahedron decomposition of the Borromean complement realises the Pentagon identity for <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_q</code> at the state-sum level. The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-3/4</code> coefficient of the Markov trace matches the difference between the 2-octahedron and 8-tetrahedron decompositions.</em></p>\n<p>The Borromean complement is the union of two regular ideal octahedra <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"adams1985hyperbolic\">[adams1985hyperbolic]</span>, and splitting each octahedron into four ideal tetrahedra around a diagonal gives an 8-tetrahedron decomposition. State sums are compared across triangulations through Pachner moves <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"pachner1991\">[pachner1991]</span>, and invariance under the 2–3 move requires <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_q</code> to satisfy the Pentagon identity. The conjecture identifies the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^4 = -3/4</code> coefficient categorically with the state-sum evaluation of this 8-tetrahedron network.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pachner-pentagon-borromean.md","heading":"Conjecture","number":"13.14.14","page":"b/conj-pachner-pentagon-borromean","qa":{"counts":{"pass":77,"fail":3,"warn":1,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":64},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:BraidKnotOctonion.PachnerPentagonBorromean","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/BraidKnotOctonion/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
